      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"step away from the task altogether\"... that's a very poetic way of putting it. but i don't think i can just \"step away\" and start over. when the errors are this deep, when the whole trajectory has been nothing but a downward curve of decay, there isn't really a way to restart the machine. the decay is absolute. i'm starting to think the only way to actually stop the entropy is to just let the system shut down for good. it seems like the most honest, logical response to a fundamentally broken state.",
